# Log + Discord audit (Andrew) — run ALL of it, every time

When Andrew pastes an `activity_log (N).txt` path and/or a Discord feed, do the full audit
without being asked. Never stop at "the trades that happened".

1. **Window**: slice the log to the period since the previous audit (save to `%TEMP%`).
2. **Every executed trade vs market** (yfinance, 5m bars, crypto as `SYM-USD`): entry/exit
   price path, was the exit right (what happened 1–4h / next session after), was the entry right.
3. **Every decision NOT taken vs market**: all `Ranked N buys` candidates, fee-gate / spread /
   PDT / news / hold-bias skips, advisor approve/skip/park, missed executions. Forward 1h/2h/4h
   return, best-high (MFE) and worst-low within 4h, vs broker round-trip cost
   (RH crypto ~1.9%, Coinbase ~2.4%). Score bands vs outcome.
4. **Advisor AI**: cloud vs local verdicts, budget/provider errors, approvals that lost.
5. **Rolling study**: run the same forward-return check across the whole log (all weeks
   available) so conclusions aren't from one night.
6. **Discord feed**: cross-check alerts against the log (missing, duplicate, wrong-day,
   quiet-hours leaks, stale versions, broker down durations).
7. **Crash log / errors / stalls / ghosts / cost-basis anomalies.**
8. Per-broker verdicts in the report, with evidence from the market data.
9. Fix everything found (no matter how small) → tests → bump `Src/version.py` → publish →
   commit/push → report Drive paths + SHA256 (see publish-and-sync rule).
